# Caddy terminates TLS and is the only container reachable from the public
# internet in a hardened deployment (see infra/docker-compose.prod.yml).
#
# It fronts the GATEWAY, not `web` -- in the Oracle VPS + Vercel topology
# (see DEPLOYMENT.md), apps/web runs on Vercel, not on this VM. Vercel's
# serverless functions run apps/web/app/api/**'s route handlers
# (apps/web/lib/gateway-client.ts), and THOSE need to reach the gateway over
# the public internet, since Vercel can't resolve this VM's Docker-internal
# service names. That call is server-to-server (Vercel's function to this
# domain), never a browser-to-gateway call, so there's no CORS to configure
# here either way.
#
# If you ever also run `web` on this same VPS instead of Vercel (fully
# self-hosted, see HOSTING.md's original walkthrough), add a second site
# block here for it and point Vercel at nothing -- don't run both fronting
# the same domain.
#
# This sslip.io hostname resolves directly to the EC2 public IP, allowing
# Caddy to obtain a publicly trusted certificate without separate DNS setup.
# Replace it with a custom API domain when one is available.

16-170-103-71.sslip.io {
	reverse_proxy gateway:4000
}
